error.message:
tool call error: tool call failed for `oxplow/oxplow_get_open_page`

Caused by:
    Mcp error: -32602: invalid input: "thread_id" is a required property. Accepted: thread_id (required), tab. Example input: {"thread_id":"thr3"}

content.text:
{
  "page": "oxplow/data-catalog",
  "title": "Data catalog",
  "params": {
    "dataset": "v_handoff"
  },
  "text": "# Data catalog [node catalog]\n| Dataset | Owner | Holds | Fields |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v_handoff | core | Work handed from one thread to another (`oxplow.handoff.send`; ref `oxplow:oxplow/handoff?id=hnd<n>`): who sent it, the thread it is for, the task it hands over, when the recipient's agent was given it, and how it ended. A record oxplow keeps, never a message it delivers: the recipient's agent is given it at its next prompt. | id INTEGER — Handoff id (`hnd<n>`). uri TEXT — `oxplow:oxplow/handoff?id=hnd<id>`: its URI, the one place SQL spells it — select and join on this, never rebuild it. from_thread_id INTEGER — The thread that sent it. from_thread_uri TEXT — That thread's URI (`oxplow:oxplow/thread?id=thr<n>`). from_session_id INTEGER — The agent session that sent it; NULL when a person or an effect did. from_session_uri TEXT — That session's URI (`oxplow:oxplow/agent_session?id=ses<n>`). from_actor TEXT — Who sent it: `user`, `agent`, `effect`, `job` or `system` (the actor, never an input). to_thread_id INTEGER — The thread it is for (never a session: the thread outlives its processes). to_thread_uri TEXT — That thread's URI: where a handoff opens. task TEXT — The task it hands over (a `task:` ref), when it names one; taking the handoff moves the item onto the recipient thread. body TEXT — Markdown body. sent_at TEXT — RFC 3339 timestamp. delivered_at TEXT — When a prompt in the recipient thread carried it to its agent; NULL until then. delivered_to_session_id INTEGER — The agent session that prompt was in. state TEXT — `open`, `taken`, `declined` (by the recipient) or `withdrawn` (by the sender). settled_at TEXT — When it was taken, declined or withdrawn; NULL while open. settled_by_session_id INTEGER — The agent session that settled it; NULL for a person. note TEXT — What its settler said, when anything. |\n\n"
}
